<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palvancha</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Paloncha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Palvancha is an industrial town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhadradri-kothagudem-district">Bhadradri Kothagudem district</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telangana">Telangana</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, near the Kinnerasani river. It was the seat of the Paloncha samasthan, a hereditary estate in the forested Godavari valley. Today it is known for the Kothagudem Thermal Power Station and other industries that draw on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a> of the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palvancha.jpg" alt="Palvancha" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Iharishs · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KTPS_at_Palvancha_03_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
